 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Depth Buffer Consistency:** If a fragment is discarded in the shader (via `kill`), the depth value of the fragment rendered last is still valid in the depth buffer. This must be accounted for when using depth tests, as the discarded fragment does not update the depth buffer [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance Overhead:** The two-pass approach introduces overhead. The initial performance loss compared to uncompressed rendering is a factor of 2-3 due to the complexity of the shaders and texture indirections [S1, unofficial].
